## 2026-10-02T12:45:34Z ci Quality (advisory) — new booking-checkout.test.ts suite failed to load
Error: [vitest] No "canonicalOrigin" export is defined on the "@/lib/site-origin" mock. Did you forget to return it from "vi.mock"?
 ❯ src/content/site.ts:13:11
 ❯ src/lib/booking-emails.ts:19:1
- resolved: The test replaced `@/lib/site-origin` wholesale, but `lib/booking-checkout.ts` pulls in `content/site.ts` (via `booking-emails.ts`), which calls `canonicalOrigin()` at import; the mock now spreads `importOriginal()` and overrides only `siteUrl`.
- rule: A vitest file that imports `web/src/lib/booking-checkout.ts` (or anything reaching `content/site.ts`) must mock `@/lib/site-origin` partially — spread `importOriginal()` — because `content/site.ts` calls `canonicalOrigin()` at module load.

## 2026-10-02T12:45:34Z ci Quality (advisory) — payment CSP test expected 'none' removed from every directive
AssertionError: object-src: expected [ '\'none\'' ] to deeply equal []
 ❯ src/lib/security-headers.test.ts:167:50
- resolved: The test's expectation was wrong, not the policy: `PAYMENT_CSP` replaces `'none'` only in directives Stripe extends (`frame-src`); the test now strips `'none'` only where it adds Stripe origins, so `object-src 'none'` is asserted to stand.
